# The pedal root's packages, beyond mmdebstrap's minbase: read by the image build (step 4 of
# docs/vip-image.md), from the pinned snapshot, without recommends. What each is for:

# The kernel: Ubuntu's RT flavour (rtpi devices/vip/device.env, PEDAL_KERNEL), and the Pi 5's
# WiFi firmware.
linux-image-7.0.0-1017-raspi-realtime
linux-modules-7.0.0-1017-raspi-realtime
linux-firmware-raspi
wireless-regdb

# Booting and the boot selection (rtpi's vip-boot: python3, dracut, the FAT tools).
systemd
systemd-sysv
systemd-resolved
systemd-timesyncd
udev
dbus
dracut-core
python3-minimal
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
# pedal-data grows to fill the card on first boot.
systemd-repart

# Reaching it.
openssh-server
sudo
wpasupplicant
iproute2
iputils-ping
ca-certificates
# scripts/sync-library copies the model and IR library with it.
rsync

# The codec (pedal-codec) and the engine's tools (alsa-utils: amixer, alsactl, arecord).
raspi-utils-dt
device-tree-compiler
alsa-utils

# pedal-tune, pedal-device, pedald (chown and stty are coreutils).
procps
util-linux
kmod
less
